  "description": "Kanye West Presents: GOOD Music – Cruel Summer, commonly referred to simply as Cruel Summer, is a compilation album by recording artists of American record label GOOD Music, released on September 14, 2012, by the label itself and its parent company, Def Jam Recordings. GOOD Music's founder, American rapper Kanye West, first revealed plans for the label's collaborative album in October 2011. It was preceded by four singles—\"Mercy\", \"Cold\", \"New God Flow\", and \"Clique\"—that saw mixed success on the US Billboard Hot 100 chart.",
